stealth.min.js is vendored (unmodified) from:

  https://github.com/jonfriesen/playwright-go-stealth v0.0.3
  (github.com/jonfriesen/playwright-go-stealth, MIT License)

Vendored directly, rather than importing the Go package, to avoid pulling in
that package's dependency on the older github.com/playwright-community/
playwright-go module -- a different Go module identity than the
github.com/mxschmitt/playwright-go module this codebase uses for everything
else (same upstream project, renamed on GitHub; see executor/browser.go's
package doc comment for why the newer module path is required here). The
stealth package's own exported surface is just this embedded JS string
(StealthJS) plus a thin Inject(page) wrapper around
page.AddInitScript(playwright.Script{Content: StealthJS}) -- vendoring the
JS file directly and calling AddInitScript ourselves reaches the exact same
behavior with one fewer transitive dependency (and its own sub-dependencies)
compiled into the binary.

